.TH BATTERY 1 "1970-1-1" "v1.0" "Custom Scripts Manuals"
.SH NAME
battery \- display battery capacity, status, and remaining time
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B battery
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B battery
is a utility script that reads power information from the 
.I macsmc-battery
interface. It provides a human-readable summary of the current charge level, 
charging state, and time estimates.
.PP
The script reformats raw seconds from the kernel into a 
.B H:MM:SS
time format for better readability.
.SH OUTPUT
The script prints the following fields to standard output:
.TP
.B Capacity
The current battery charge percentage.
.TP
.B Status
The current power state (e.g., Charging, Discharging, Full, or Not charging).
.TP
.B Estimated time until empty/full
Displayed only when the battery is actively discharging or charging. 
It shows the time remaining in 
.B H:MM:SS
format. If the data is unavailable or zero, it returns 
.B N/A .
.SH FILES
The script reads data from the following sysfs paths:
.TP
.I /sys/class/power_supply/macsmc-battery/capacity
Current battery charge percentage.
.TP
.I /sys/class/power_supply/macsmc-battery/status
Current charging state.
.TP
.I /sys/class/power_supply/macsmc-battery/time_to_empty_now
Raw seconds remaining until the battery is depleted.
.TP
.I /sys/class/power_supply/macsmc-battery/time_to_full_now
Raw seconds remaining until the battery is fully charged.
.SH NOTES
This script is specifically configured for systems using the 
.B macsmc-battery 
driver (common on Linux on Apple Silicon). It may require modification 
to work with standard 
.B BAT0 
interfaces.
.SH SEE ALSO
.MR printf 1 ,
.MR bash 1
